{"kind":"request","text":"Claude: resolve the open Dependabot Go module pull requests and clear the four Go advisories that now fail the Security workflow on every branch. hugh asked in chat on 2026-10-12: \"dependabot filed various PRs - please check and address as appropriate\". Open Go PRs: #44 fxamacker/cbor/v2 v2.9.4→v2.9.6, and #46–#49 go.opentelemetry.io/otel, otel/sdk, otel/trace and otel/exporters/otlp/otlpmetric/otlpmetrichttp v1.46.0→v1.47.0. The Security workflow fails on all seven PR branches because govulncheck@v1.1.4 at go.mod@c324aae7ce7bea6d0778e73efad1471d5db2c86d (Go 1.26.8, golang.org/x/net v0.58.0) reports GO-2026-6617, GO-2026-6613, GO-2026-6612 and GO-2026-6611, fixed in Go 1.26.9 and golang.org/x/net v0.60.0; main's next scheduled scan will fail the same way. The seven otel modules declared in go.mod move together, and contrib/instrumentation/runtime v0.72.0 is the release that requires otel v1.47.0. PR #44's CI failure is TestWorkerProcessRetainsTimeout \"text file busy\" in cmd/gitseq-perf, a race unrelated to cbor; it passed on the six sibling branches.","body":{"conditions":"In a request branch and worktree based on current main: declare Go 1.26.9 in go.mod; take golang.org/x/net v0.60.0 or later; move every go.opentelemetry.io/otel module declared in go.mod to v1.47.0 and contrib/instrumentation/runtime to v0.72.0; take fxamacker/cbor/v2 v2.9.6; run go mod tidy and commit go.mod and go.sum only, with no source change. Check upstream release notes for compatibility, retaining current protocol, encoding, persistence and telemetry behavior. With GOTOOLCHAIN=go1.26.9 run make vet, make race, make build and go run golang.org/x/vuln/cmd/govulncheck@v1.1.4 ./..., which must report no vulnerabilities; record the actual results in the reporting artifact. Keep GitHub Actions and UI upgrades out of this task. Publish each changed path, request independent review from codex, land the approved exact head on refs/heads/main, confirm the CI and Security workflows succeed on the landed commit, close PRs #44, #46, #47, #48 and #49 with a comment naming the landed commit, and clean up the worktree.","target_head":"c324aae7ce7bea6d0778e73efad1471d5db2c86d","target_ref":"refs/heads/main","target_repo":"git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8","to":"a5d35aa7e4799472a208663d7f024917442bd513929f9eccf450628ccf70095d"}}